  "annotations_dropped": [
    {
      "annotation_id": "8920931d9673463aaec1aeef883e6fa0_98",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "13. Before dwelling into the facts of the present case, it would be apt to discuss the legal standards required to be met by both sides."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c32b9c933ead494d8c85f7dfdce958c0_99",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In criminal law, the burden of proving the guilt of the accused exclusively lies on the prosecution which must prove the offence charged beyond reasonable doubt."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e2ddd091f35a472cb31011bd3cf2862f_100",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe benefit of doubt, if any, must go in favour of the accused."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0f5d78b6091b4e1e8c2b5a6deaf645e5_101",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n14. Section 188 IPC provides punishment for disobedience to order duly promulgated by public servant despite knowledge of such order."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3e2fd39055504adea0548628cb7d5b58_102",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 269, IPC punishes whoever unlawfully or negligently does any act which is, and which he knows or has reason to believe to be, likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b812a3526848494cbfe0a4df8c3a4610_103",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 270 IPC punishes whoever malignantly does any act which is, and which he knows or has reason the believe to be, likely to spread the infection of any disease NEHA Date:\nBARUPAL 2024.07.18 16:14:48 +0530 dangerous to life."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4f9deb6230e940c3b173706237d42126_104",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 3 of Epidemic Diseases Act, 1897 provides, inter alia, that any person disobeying any regulation or order made under this Act shall be deemed to have committed an offence punishable under section 188 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860.\n"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ab0ef788ae4a47789c487e5fbe517aa5_105",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the present case, the accused has been charged with, inter alia, offence under section 188 IPC for selling vegetables at his shop without any sign board for prevention of Corona (COVID-19)\nduring lockdown in violation of order under sect"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "25b767b7eb314177a40655d80d36ce8f_106",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "16. The following essential ingredients of the offence under Section 188 IPC have been highlighted by the Division Bench of the Hon'ble High Court of Delhi in Bhoop Singh Tyagi v. State 2002 SCC OnLine Del 277 - 1) there must be an order pr"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2e807bc5cd3848549010cf4fcca01b73_107",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n2) such public servant must be lawfully empowered to promulgate such order."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1b0fda4f379e4c1c933eba4dda55c5aa_108",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n3) A person must have a knowledge of such order directing him to abstain from an act or (b) to take certain order with certain property in his possession or under his management."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d52e2f4afad349088c166b09fa1f2315_109",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "State vs Omar Farooq@Amar on 18 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/196977861/"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "589032dc2468446aa72787d836b9175a_110",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n5 4) He must disobey the order having its knowledge."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1b40964eb69b4cf2bb5268046b897650_111",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n5) Such obedience must cause or tend to cause (a) obstruction, annoyance or injury or risk of it to any person lawfully employ or (b) danger to human life, health and safety.\"\n17."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "71f2a8faea124d5395e0f29dbcb450bf_112",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, all the above-mentioned ingredients are to be proved in order to prove the commission of said offence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "97bfc9a8e0b843be8f6a9ee0c0bcab1e_113",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "To determine whether the accused is liable in this case, it is pertinent to NEHA BARUPAL BARUPAL Date:\n2024.07.18 16:14:56 +0530 examine the directions in the aforesaid order."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "6a6bf71663854df6b161cb847c701c64_114",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The order prohibited the following acts: -\n(1) Assembly of any kind for demonstrations, processions, protests etc."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8b0a015891584a43a7175e18e8958f82_115",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "(2) Any gathering social /clutural /political /religious /academic/ sports /seminar /conference (3) Organization of weekly markets (except for vegetables, fruits and essential commodities), concerts, exhibitions etc."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7b475e0ad6874a4691091a88c15bf007_116",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "(4) Guided group tours conducted by various private tour operators (5) Any individual suspected/confirmed with COVID-19 shall take measures for prevention/treatment i.e. home quarantine/institution quarantine/ isolation or any such person s"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "333c00c6df6e4cccaa26b66fbabb2d38_117",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n(6) Any person contravening this order shall be punishable under section 188 of Indian Penal Code."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d3c4f6580d9b4710b1c09cd7e06dd1e0_118",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "18. In the present case, it is evident from the above that the order, the violation of which has been alleged, nowhere prohibited the accused from selling vegetables, rather it carved out an exception for selling of vegetables, fruits and e"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "571c68104f1242f1aeff15bfb8ef9998_119",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Admittedly, as stated by PW3, during COVID-19 the Government had notified an order to run the shops pertaining to essential commodities on odd and even scheme."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b94a7101b8f4455aa49dae096c288f19_120",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The accused in his defence evidence has also proved the relevant order of Agricultural Produce Marketing Committee Fruit & Vegetable Market (Sub-Yard Okhla, New Delhi-20) no. APMC/Okhla/130 dated 12.04.2020 (Ex. DW1/1) which provides that e"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "68650b6ca7794247a07830893c96d459_121",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Although the case of the prosecution is not that the accused was not entitled to open his shop on the concerned date, the prosecution was required to prove violation of an order or regulation in order to prove the charge but it was unsucces"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a91de64343ca4e7faf0da195724f23f3_122",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Furthermore, the abovesaid order of ACP does not reflect that the accused was under any obligation to put up a sign board for prevention of Corona (COVID-19)."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ee680763992244edb1d02b9209a1ec9c_123",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThus, in the absence of proof of existence of order mandating the accused to display the sign board as alleged, the accused certainly cannot be held guilty for violation of any such order."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "65940d92ab9144cea9c0cfdd60801ee9_124",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "19. Similarly, no regulation or order under Epidemic Diseases Act, 1897 has been filed by/relied upon by the prosecution for the violation of which the accused may be convicted."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b6d2363771f9489aa49e2ebf7b628322_125",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nState vs Omar Farooq@Amar on 18 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/196977861/\n6 20."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "01774f2762e4421a8351e049422c7c7d_126",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the instant case, no evidence has come to light showing malicious intention of the accused, let alone higher degree of malice or evil that is required for commission of the offence under section 270 IPC which uses the words \"whoever mali"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d219841d53484e1298255a5c0eaa3180_127",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In addition, no such act has been attributed to the accused which he knew or had reason to believe would lead to spreading the infection of any disease dangerous to life."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "17463e0edf734d6cb5577012ede4bc32_128",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus, charge under section 270 IPC also remains unsubstantiated."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a32eeb61a1f74273852bd1d55757c5c1_129",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "STA"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "21. For proving the commission of offence under section 269 IPC, unlawful or negligent conduct of the accused which is, and which the accused knows or has reason to believe is likely to spread the infection of any disease dangerous to life,"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "fb3fd195df5f445f82a135614986c274_130",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, such unlawful or negligent conduct has not been proved by the documentary and oral evidence in this case."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "dab89b730b934811a020055067acb3c6_131",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The reasons for the aforesaid finding are discussed below."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a6fc13d7aeab4a98bd06ad60ef7fd7c4_132",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "22. It is pertinent to note that there are glaring inconsistencies/weaknesses in the prosecution case, starting with the date of the alleged incident."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ea270aa390bd488c9e1faba7202b4b5e_133",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The complaint (Ex.\nPW2/A) on the basis of which FIR was lodged against the accused is itself inconsistent."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4c03d0d02f704376b982dbf58c05151e_134",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It mentions that the incident is of 23.04.2020 whereas at the bottom of the said complaint, the date of incident is mentioned at 27.02.2020."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "61df84d6a2dc41f5b22432873c765bea_135",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Complicating the matter further, the prosecution witnesses have deposed that the incident is of 27.04.2020."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a7067f4675bc438ab154540a823a87f1_136",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, it is crystal clear that there is a major doubt regarding the date of the incident itself, leading this court to doubt even the commission of the offence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "44fed2621d864289b45fb6874df88a5c_137",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The information was allegedly given vide DD no. 3A at 1:05 am on 28.04.2020 however no such DD entry has been placed on record."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "89c211844b2b45dbbfc5c15502ca89f0_138",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The complaint under section 195 CrPC mentions that the concerned officers were on patrolling duty on 28.04.2020 when they reached the shop of the accused and saw the offence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "934807efe5474e32be40783014be9cca_139",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The statement of Ct. Rakesh under section 161 CrPC also mentions the date of 23.04.2020."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c69051be215046f99f23edfc0fa8c977_140",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Even the name of the accused has been incorrectly mentioned in the chargesheet."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "84c8f9a73f2e4e58878e65a05aa87b1c_141",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "23. It is also worth noting that there is no evidence on record in the form of photographs to show that the accused had not displayed the requisite sign board on his shop as alleged."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7b1a28f7bc1844b68597c763079dd6ae_142",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The official(s) could have easily taken photograph of the shop when NEHA BARUPAL BARUPAL Date:\n2024.07.18 16:15:23 +0530 he/they noticed that such sign board has not been displayed and they could have filed the same along with the chargeshe"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0b77f170affd4a39a38f09f7ddbb0303_143",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus, in view of the above discussed facts and circumstances of the case, this court finds that the prosecution has failed to prove the commission of the offences by the accused on the threshold of beyond reasonable doubt."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "f23a0231b65a444b855dad2f15be8740_144",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The general principles of criminal jurisprudence, namely, that the prosecution has to prove its case beyond reasonable doubt and that the accused is entitled to the benefit of a reasonable doubt,\nState vs Omar Farooq@Amar on 18 July, 2024 I"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "e424bbaab883467d896eb80bdcfaa1b0_145",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As the prosecution has failed to establish the essential ingredients of the alleged offence, the prosecution case does not stand on its legs."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "770eec725cb644f5ae4fc4d8bf6f672e_146",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "25. On the other hand, the accused has been successful in pointing out the deficiencies in the case of the prosecution."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3e4bb267ce5c4f61a15279d4b8ba4818_147",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "26. Consequently, accused Omar Farooq @ Amar is acquitted of the offences under section 188/269/270 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 and section 3 of Epidemic Diseases Act, 1897."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2e935ff6df544f69af56f90561681edf_148",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "ORDER - ACQUITTED Pronounced in open court on 18.07.2024."
    }
  ],
